WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.600
[Music]

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:55.340
[Group of elderly people have gathered and are socializing outside.]

00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:03.820
[Narrator:] We all know people like these: former neighbors, old friends, relatives.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:09.460
Three are so many of them, so many chronically ill and aged in this country.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.800
Almost six million invalids.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Many of them without ordinary and often vitally-needed dental care.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.520
Fortunately more and more attention
is now being focused on their plight

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.780
and dentists are discovering that the
principle difference between routine treatments

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.800
and invalid treatments lies in the management of the patient.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.220
Dentists' experience shows that treatment
of the homebound and infirm

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:46.400
requires no highly specialized training and only a minimum of easy-to-carry portable equipment.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.000
No more on each trip than
needed for the case at hand.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:57.000
By properly positioning the patient at
the side of a hospital bed

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.640
or with a partial back rest on a regular bed,
and placing the hand equipment

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:05.870
on a table found in the patient's own room, ease and convenience of operation is assured.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:14.000
For this case, note that the dentist is using a portable high-speed air turbine, powered by a small bottle of CO2.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.480
[Music]

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.820
Who are the chronically ill?

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:23.540
They can be simply defined as people with long-term disabling illnesses,

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:28.900
including arthritis, diabetes, multiple sclerosis, heart disease, palsy, and many other diseases.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.620
[Music]

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:39.000
Most chronically ill and aged people can, with assistance, visit a clinic or office for dental treatment.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.160
In such cases, with regular office equipment

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.660
and the dentist's own dental assistant, there are only minor differences between

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:50.780
treating most chronically ill patients
and routine patients.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.180
[Music]

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:58.060
With patients who cannot visit an office or clinic, the need for portable equipment is obvious.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:06.560
To help dentists meet the needs of such patients, portable equipment was studied along with other aspects of dental care for the chronically ill,

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.140
in a four-year research program by the United States Public Health Service.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:15.080
The study disclosed that complete and satisfactory dental care can be given in the home

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:18.580
with various types of currently
available portable equipment.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:21.040
[Music]

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.480
For example, this completely
self-contained luggage case unit

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.480
weighing less than 40 pounds and powered
from a standard hundred and ten volt wall outlet,

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:35.400
includes a standard speed motor, aspirator, compressed air water spray, and gooseneck lamp.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.000
Such units have wide versatility.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:43.520
In this case the unit is supplemented by a
headrest that can be clamped on an ordinary chair.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.920
The dentist takes with him on home calls

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.100
only a minimum of instruments and supplies carried in any handy carrying case that can be laid out

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.500
conveniently on a small table found in
the patient's own home.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:04:02.880
[Music]

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:08.400
This is a typical home care situation. In practically every instance, by using available furniture,

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:13.020
equipment and instruments can be located
as conveniently as in office situations.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.960
[Music]

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:20.040
The dentist knew in advance that this
patient would require local anesthesia,

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:25.100
so disposable cartridge and needle were
included in the kit of instruments for this call.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:41.820
[Music]

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:46.460
As in the office, the dental assistant
acts as a second pair of hands for the dentist,

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:50.000
helping reduce the time required to treat the patient.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:05:10.840
[Music]

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:14.660
All that remains now is the preliminary
trimming of the restoration

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.020
and of course polishing at the next visit.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:24.000
The completed restoration is fully comparable to work done with standard office equipment.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.700
Total time elapsed  from setting up to leaving the house, 30 minutes,

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.960
only slightly longer than the office time for similar work.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.780
[Music]

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:37.600
Other types of dental treatment can be provided equally well in the home.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:42.020
In this case the dental hygienist is completing a prophylaxis with portable equipment

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:47.700
that clamps directly to the wheelchair, headrest, motor, and gooseneck lamp.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:51.200
After the prophylaxis she will show the patient how to brush his teeth properly

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.300
and suggest dietary considerations to help him maintain a good dental health.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.920
[Music]

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:04.000
At a later visit the dentist comes prepared for an extraction with just the equipment and instruments required.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:08.400
The headrest is clamped on the wheelchair
and for convenience in this instance

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.880
the dentist uses a headlight instead of a
clamp-on gooseneck light.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:17.980
[Music]

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:21.320
The needed sterile instruments are laid
out on a table found in the patient's room

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:25.040
alongside the aspirator that's
plugged into a wall outlet.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:31.000
The assistant removes blood and moisture
with a portable surgical aspirator as in office chair-side assistance.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:37.780
[Music]

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:40.780
After the extraction the used
instruments are carefully wrapped in

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:44.170
putting the carrying case for return to
the office where they will be sterilized.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:48.040
Again the entire procedure has been
little different from office methods

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:52.820
except for the use of the minimum of
portable equipment required for the visit.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:56.820
[Music]

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:59.960
The full range of dental
treatment is possible in home care cases

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:05.000
This patient has had 12 extractions,
alveoloplasty, impressions,

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:09.000
and vertical [?] while confined to her bed,

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:14.200
a hospital-type bed, as is the case with many long-term chronically ill patients.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.940
[Music]

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:19.000
On this visit her dentures will be inserted.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.020
Dentures are important to
this patient for more than health reasons.

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:28.000
Most people confined by chronic
illness greatly need the lift attention gives them.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:29.800
The feeling that somebody cares.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.120
The pleasure of eating a variety of foods.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:35.920
[Music]

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:40.260
In addition the dentures will do much to
restore her self-confidence

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:43.500
and help her enjoy the company of her family and friends.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.800
The equipment for adjusting her dentures is simple.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.300
In this case the dentures are relieved with a standard stone and a portable hand-motor tool.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.690
And to achieve proper occlusion,

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:58.800
the tooth surfaces are ground and polished with the same motor tool using a standard dental wheel.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:11.400
[Music]

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:15.300
Each step in the making of this patient's
dentures was performed in her home:

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:20.960
extractions, impressions, bite registration, and of course fitting of the completed dentures.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:35.680
[Music]

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:41.080
Prosthetics, extractions, restorations,
oral surgery, periodontal treatment...

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:46.200
a complete range of dental care can be
administered to the chronically ill in their homes

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:50.400
with only slight modification of the operating techniques used in the office.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:54.900
[Music]

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.400
Where then are the differences?

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:00.920
Primarily in the management of the patient and in evaluating her dental needs.

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:03.660
[Music]

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:09.260
Whether the patient is in her home or more commonly in the dentist's own office or in the clinic,

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:13.120
dental care is generally a special event
to the chronically ill.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:29.900
[Music]

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:36.000
Good rapport can usually be obtained by
making the patient feel the appointment is a special event for the dentist too.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:40.200
[Music]

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:44.519
The chronically ill and aged often have a
lower tolerance to pain and discomfort.

00:09:44.519 --> 00:09:47.900
By allowing patients to rest frequently
and breaking up the treatment

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:52.000
into shorter periods, undue fatigue and
tension can be avoided.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:59.300
It is also important to bolster the patient's
confidence, complimenting her generously on each accomplishment.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:02.900
This approach is applicable of course to any patient of any age group.

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:05.120
[Music]

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:11.220
However, younger chronically ill patients are often more conscious of the extra effort that dentist must make to treat them.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:13.980
And therefore more obviously
appreciative.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:16.460
[Music]

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:20.660
But no matter what the patient's age, the reassurance that the dentist personally cares enough

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:24.880
to provide the treatments helps lighten the
heavy emotional burden of chronic illness.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:26.880
[Music]

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:30.120
Many chronically ill patients
will also be receiving medical treatment

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:33.320
and the dentist may wish to consult with
a patient's physician.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.740
[Music]

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:41.900
It is important to have at least a brief
medical history so the need for consultation can be judged.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:51.500
[Music]

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:55.760
A typical medical history should include
medical diagnosis of the patient's illness,

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:59.000
medication, and the name of the
patient's physician.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:04.250
With general questions covering fainting, excessive bleeding, reactions from penicillin or anesthetics,

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:09.700
sores that heal slowly and other general symptoms that might require consultation.

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:18.160
[Music]

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:22.900
Medical consultation is indicated
particularly for heart patients

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:29.020
or for patients on anticoagulant drugs when extractions or deep curettage are required.

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:34.460
[Music]

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:39.020
Patients receiving corticosteroids for
conditions such as rheumatoid arthritis,

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:44.260
ulcerative colitis, or a blood dyscrasia
may be susceptible to post-operative infections.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:48.880
For such patients, prophylactic use of antibiotics may be indicated.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.820
[Music]

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:58.000
Medical consultation is usually necessary for diabetic patients before even minor dental procedures.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.740
So routine but necessary precautions may be taken.

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:04.140
Although most patients can be treated in the office or home,

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:07.260
hospitalization is sometimes required for patients

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:12.140
with severe circulatory diseases, diabetes, and extensive oral malignancies.

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:14.540
[Music]

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:18.580
Criteria for treatment must be evaluated along with several other aspects of the patient's condition.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:20.900
[Music]

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:23.600
One such factor is the patient's general physical health.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:26.440
For example when long-term systemic disorders

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:31.900
have lowered general resistance, dentures may cause deterioration of the oral mucosa and tissues.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:33.900
[Music]

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:35.950
In other patients periodontal disease may have reduced

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:39.880
supporting bone structures so the
denture success is questionable.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:46.120
Severe periodontal disease is not uncommon with the chronically ill and aged, since their oral hygiene is often poorly maintained.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:49.440
[Music]

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:52.060
The psychological attitude of the
patient is very important.

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:54.580
[Music]

00:12:54.720 --> 00:13:01.840
If the patient has adjusted well to chronic illness, as this patient has, his positive attitude may override many adverse indications.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:05.800
The most important consideration is the potential benefit to the patient.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.900
As can be seen, the portable equipment is light enough for easy handling.

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:12.980
[Music]

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:19.100
The responsibility for providing the chronically ill and aged with dental care falls on the entire community.

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:24.160
It is shared by the aged and chronically ill
who must make an effort to obtain care.

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:27.520
[Music]

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:32.100
It is shared by the dentist who must be
prepared to treat the chronically ill and aged.

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:36.720
It is shared by the
professional schools that must prepare

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:42.000
future dentists and hygienists to treat
the chronically ill as a routine part of dental practice.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.940
Whether in the office or
in the home.

00:13:43.940 --> 00:13:47.040
[Music]

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:53.900
The University of Kansas City School of Dentistry, for example, participated in the Public Health Service study of dental care for the chronically ill.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:14:02.800
The classroom training of dental and dental hygiene students was supplemented by practice in private and nursing homes.

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.000
[Music]

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.000
The result?

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:10.000
Dental care for many people who otherwise would not have been treated,

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:15.500
and training for the students in situations 
significantly different from the clinic or standard dental office.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:21.480
We asked Dr. Hamilton B.G. Robinson, Dean of the School of Dentistry at the University of Kansas City,

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:26.140
for his evaluation of the training program. Dr. Robinson.

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:32.140
[Dr. Robinson:] Our dental students and our dental hygiene students have both benefited greatly from this program.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:37.300
They used the portable equipment. They learned to handle the patients,

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:43.320
and above allthey learned the great need that these patients have for dental care.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:48.430
In cooperation with the Public Health
Service, we are incorporating treatment

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:53.900
of the chronically ill and aged in the
curricula of our dental and dental hygiene schools.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:59.000
This means expanding our present courses in home care

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:04.660
and may involve auxiliary training centers at nursing homes willing to cooperate with us.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:10.000
Other dental schools of course are
working on similar plans,

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:16.000
and we would like to feel that within the next five or six years, every new dentist

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:22.000
and every new dental hygienist will enter practice prepared to take care of the chronically ill and aged.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:29.900
And that they will also expect that they will have patients who require complete dental care in their own homes.

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:36.680
[Narrator:] In the meantime, it remains for the dentists of today to add a new dimension to their general practice of dentistry.

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:41.240
Many of the chronically ill an aged fit into normal office routine.

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:46.180
The Kansas City project and other studies reached several clear conclusions.

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:52.840
Among them, the chronically ill and aged can be treated at home or in the office with no highly specialized training

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:59.600
and with only slight modification of
operating techniques, treatment criteria, and equipment.

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:04.100
Management of such patients requires a heightened sensitivity of a patient as an individual.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:07.840
[Music]

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:13.100
Chair-side assistance can of course help speed the dentist's work in both home and office treatment.

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:15.340
[Music]

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:19.779
The dental hygienist can perform prophylaxis, give oral hygiene instruction

00:16:19.779 --> 00:16:26.100
and devise adaptations and modifications of standard devices that enable the patient to maintain better oral hygiene.

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:29.890
[Music]

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:34.400
Most types of treatment can be
administered either in the office or home.

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:36.400
[Music]

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:40.700
When there is a choice, treatment
should be given in a dental office or clinic.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:44.620
But sometimes there is no choice
and the dental service must be taken to the patient.

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:51.900
Home care patients can be given the same complete dental care as office patients, using portable equipment.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:56.000
Such equipment might be obtained by the local Dental Society Health Department

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:59.000
or other agencies for the use of all dentists.

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:02.000
[Music]

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:07.900
Although dental care for the chronically
ill and aged may involve a little extra time and effort.

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:13.200
It yields a deep and rewarding satisfaction, for the burden of chronic illness and age

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:19.700
is a burden of loneliness and isolation filled with problems and worries unfamiliar to most of us.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:23.380
Lack of dental care should not be one of these worries.

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:30.920
[Music]

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:35.900
It is not only practical and feasible to provide the aged and chronically ill with dental care.

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:39.900
It is the ethical and moral obligation of the dental profession.

00:17:39.900 --> 00:18:10.000
[Music]

